# 6) Lightweight proof-of-concept scaffolding

Below is a minimal TypeScript-style scaffold showing how hooks, policy metadata, templates, and rendering can fit together.

## A. Domain models
```ts
type UUID = string;

type PolicyEnvelope = {
  provenance: Provenance;
  rights: RightsMetadata;
  restrictions: RestrictionMetadata;
  moderation: ModerationMetadata;
};

type Asset = {
  id: UUID;
  kind: "image" | "video" | "audio" | "text" | "vector";
  mimeType: string;
  uri: string;
  width?: number;
  height?: number;
  durationMs?: number;
  metadata: Record<string, any>;
  policy: PolicyEnvelope;
};

type Template = {
  id: UUID;
  name: string;
  slots: TemplateSlot[];
  sceneBlueprints: Scene[];
  policyProfile?: string;
};

type ProjectInstance = {
  id: UUID;
  templateId?: UUID;
  scenes: Scene[];
  slotBindings: Record<string, any>;
  policy: PolicyEnvelope;
};
```

---

## B. Hook system
```ts
type HookName =
  | "beforeUpload"
  | "afterUpload"
  | "onMetadataExtracted"
  | "beforeSlotBind"
  | "beforePreviewRender"
  | "beforeExport"
  | "onPolicyViolation";

type HookContext = {
  userId: string;
  asset?: Asset;
  template?: Template;
  project?: ProjectInstance;
  renderContext?: RenderContext;
  payload?: any;
};

type HookHandler = (ctx: HookContext) => Promise<void>;

class HookRegistry {
  private handlers: Record<string, HookHandler[]> = {};

  register(name: HookName, handler: HookHandler) {
    if (!this.handlers[name]) this.handlers[name] = [];
    this.handlers[name].push(handler);
  }

  async run(name: HookName, ctx: HookContext) {
    for (const handler of this.handlers[name] || []) {
      await handler(ctx);
    }
  }
}
```

---

## C. Policy enforcement example
```ts
class PolicyEngine {
  validateAssetForSlot(asset: Asset, slot: TemplateSlot): string[] {
    const issues: string[] = [];

    if (
      slot.constraints.allowedMimeTypes &&
      !slot.constraints.allowedMimeTypes.includes(asset.mimeType)
    ) {
      issues.push("mime_type_not_allowed");
    }

    if (
      slot.constraints.maxDurationMs &&
      asset.durationMs &&
      asset.durationMs > slot.constraints.maxDurationMs
    ) {
      issues.push("duration_exceeds_slot_limit");
    }

    if (
      slot.constraints.moderationProfile === "general-audience" &&
      asset.policy.restrictions.audience !== "general"
    ) {
      issues.push("asset_not_allowed_for_general_audience");
    }

    if (asset.policy.moderation.status === "blocked") {
      issues.push("asset_blocked");
    }

    return issues;
  }

  validateProjectForRender(project: ProjectInstance, ctx: RenderContext): string[] {
    const issues: string[] = [];
    if (
      ctx.outputMode === "video-export" &&
      project.policy.restrictions.noExternalShare
    ) {
      issues.push("project_cannot_be_exported");
    }
    return issues;
  }
}
```

---

## D. Safe template binding
```ts
function sanitizeText(input: string): string {
  return input.replace(/[<>]/g, "");
}

class TemplateBinder {
  constructor(private policyEngine: PolicyEngine, private hooks: HookRegistry) {}

  async bindSlot(
    userId: string,
    template: Template,
    slotId: string,
    value: any
  ) {
    const slot = template.slots.find(s => s.id === slotId);
    if (!slot) throw new Error("slot_not_found");

    await this.hooks.run("beforeSlotBind", {
      userId,
      template,
      payload: { slot, value }
    });

    if (slot.kind === "text") {
      return sanitizeText(String(value));
    }

    if (slot.kind === "image" || slot.kind === "video" || slot.kind === "audio") {
      const asset = value as Asset;
      const issues = this.policyEngine.validateAssetForSlot(asset, slot);
      if (issues.length) {
        throw new Error(`slot_binding_rejected:${issues.join(",")}`);
      }
      return asset.id;
    }

    return value;
  }
}
```

---

## E. Renderer abstraction
```ts
type ValidationIssue = { code: string; message: string };

type RenderResult = {
  type: "interactive" | "video";
  outputUri?: string;
  warnings?: ValidationIssue[];
};

interface RendererAdapter {
  validate(scene: Scene, ctx: RenderContext): ValidationIssue[];
  renderScene(scene: Scene, ctx: RenderContext): Promise<RenderResult>;
}

class HtmlPreviewRenderer implements RendererAdapter {
  validate(scene: Scene, ctx: RenderContext): ValidationIssue[] {
    const issues: ValidationIssue[] = [];
    if (ctx.accessibility.highContrast) {
      // perform contrast-related checks if theme known
    }
    return issues;
  }

  async renderScene(scene: Scene, ctx: RenderContext): Promise<RenderResult> {
    // POC: would convert scene graph to DOM/CSS instructions
    return {
      type: "interactive",
      warnings: this.validate(scene, ctx)
    };
  }
}

class VideoExportRenderer implements RendererAdapter {
  validate(scene: Scene, ctx: RenderContext): ValidationIssue[] {
    return [];
  }

  async renderScene(scene: Scene, ctx: RenderContext): Promise<RenderResult> {
    // POC: would serialize scene graph to ffmpeg/webcodecs pipeline
    return {
      type: "video",
      outputUri: `/exports/${scene.id}.mp4`
    };
  }
}
```

---

## F. Accessibility adaptation
```ts
function adaptSceneForAccessibility(scene: Scene, ctx: RenderContext): Scene {
  if (!ctx.accessibility.reducedMotion) return scene;

  return {
    ...scene,
    timeline: scene.timeline.map(track => ({
      ...track,
      keyframes: track.keyframes.length
        ? [track.keyframes[0], track.keyframes[track.keyframes.length - 1]]
        : []
    }))
  };
}
```

---

## G. Composition service orchestration
```ts
class CompositionService {
  constructor(
    private hooks: HookRegistry,
    private policyEngine: PolicyEngine,
    private previewRenderer: RendererAdapter,
    private exportRenderer: RendererAdapter
  ) {}

  async previewProject(userId: string, project: ProjectInstance, ctx: RenderContext) {
    await this.hooks.run("beforePreviewRender", { userId, project, renderContext: ctx });

    const policyIssues = this.policyEngine.validateProjectForRender(project, ctx);
    if (policyIssues.length) {
      await this.hooks.run("onPolicyViolation", {
        userId,
        project,
        payload: policyIssues
      });
      throw new Error(policyIssues.join(","));
    }

    const scene = adaptSceneForAccessibility(project.scenes[0], ctx);
    return this.previewRenderer.renderScene(scene, ctx);
  }

  async exportProject(userId: string, project: ProjectInstance, ctx: RenderContext) {
    await this.hooks.run("beforeExport", { userId, project, renderContext: ctx });

    const policyIssues = this.policyEngine.validateProjectForRender(project, {
      ...ctx,
      outputMode: "video-export"
    });

    if (policyIssues.length) {
      await this.hooks.run("onPolicyViolation", {
        userId,
        project,
        payload: policyIssues
      });
      throw new Error(policyIssues.join(","));
    }

    const scene = adaptSceneForAccessibility(project.scenes[0], ctx);
    return this.exportRenderer.renderScene(scene, {
      ...ctx,
      outputMode: "video-export"
    });
  }
}
```

---

## H. Example hook registrations
```ts
const hooks = new HookRegistry();

hooks.register("beforeUpload", async ({ payload }) => {
  if (!payload?.mimeType) throw new Error("missing_mime_type");
});

hooks.register("beforeSlotBind", async ({ payload }) => {
  const { slot, value } = payload;
  if (slot.kind === "text" && String(value).length > 120) {
    throw new Error("text_too_long");
  }
});

hooks.register("beforeExport", async ({ project }) => {
  if (project?.policy.moderation.status === "review") {
    throw new Error("project_under_review");
  }
});
```

---

# 7) Technical design recommendations by challenge area

## A. For seamless user customization
- Use template slots with constraints
- Keep source assets immutable
- Store edits as declarative diffs
- Support real-time preview using same scene graph as export
- Build autosave/versioning from event stream
- Offer guardrails, not rigid locks

## B. For moderation and expression balance
- Use graduated restrictions instead of binary deletion
- Moderate both assets and compositions
- Keep human review path for ambiguous cases
- Make policy explainable to users
- Allow appeals and revision workflows
- Separate discoverability restrictions from possession restrictions where legally possible

## C. For provenance and ownership
- Every asset/project/export gets a persistent ID
- Track derivations and transformations
- Store rights metadata separately from display metadata but linked tightly
- Optionally embed export manifests/signatures
- Preserve attribution in downstream exports where required

## D. For highly visual rendering
- Use renderer adapters
- Render from a normalized scene graph
- Avoid renderer-specific logic in project data
- Design context-aware layout resolution
- Support responsive text fitting and localization expansion
- Build thumbnail/poster generation as first-class outputs

## E. For dynamic templates/inputs
- Restrict template expressions to a safe DSL
- Validate all inputs against schemas
- Resolve variables in deterministic order
- Provide fallback values and slot-level defaults
- Allow conditional content using whitelisted rules only

---

# 8) Likely technology choices

Depending on scale and stack preferences:

## Frontend/editor
- React + TypeScript
- Canvas/WebGL via PixiJS, Konva, Fabric, or custom renderer
- Remotion-like ideas for timeline composition
- ProseMirror/Slate for rich text overlays
- Web Audio API for timeline preview

## Backend
- Node/TypeScript, Go, or Python services
- Postgres for relational data
- S3-compatible object storage
- Redis for jobs/cache
- Kafka/SNS/SQS/NATS for events
- FFmpeg/WebCodecs/render workers for exports

## Moderation/accessibility
- OCR/ASR pipelines
- CV/NLP moderation classifiers
- contrast and flashing analyzers
- transcript generation + editing support

---

# 9) Important failure modes to design for

1. **Policy drift**
   - old exports remain public after restrictions change
   - solve with revocation hooks and derivative tracking

2. **Renderer mismatch**
   - preview differs from export
   - solve with shared canonical scene graph and parity tests

3. **Template abuse**
   - arbitrary scripts or malicious embeds
   - solve with declarative templates, schema validation, sandboxing

4. **Localization/layout breakage**
   - text expansion ruins scenes
   - solve with responsive text layout and validation

5. **Moderation blind spots**
   - asset individually safe, composition not safe
   - solve with scene-level moderation

6. **Accessibility regressions**
   - flashy template updates slip through
   - solve with automated checks in lifecycle hooks

7. **Rights confusion**
   - licensed asset reused outside scope
   - solve with rights-aware slot enforcement and export checks

---

# 10) A concise reference architecture

## Canonical flow
- User uploads asset
- Asset service stores source, generates derivatives, extracts metadata
- Policy engine annotates asset with moderation/provenance/restrictions
- User selects template
- Template binder validates slot inputs
- Project scene graph is instantiated with user variables
- Preview renderer produces interactive result
- Export renderer creates video/image package
- Export manifest captures provenance and restrictions
- Discovery layer only surfaces policy-approved outputs

---

# 11) Final takeaway

A strong design for this kind of platform should be built around:

- a **declarative scene graph**
- **template slots with constraints**
- **renderer adapters**
- **lifecycle hooks**
- **policy/accessibility metadata envelopes**
- **lineage/provenance tracking**
- **graduated moderation enforcement**
- **context-aware rendering**

That combination gives you a system that is:
- modular
- extensible
- safe
- customizable
- exportable
- explainable
- suitable for highly visual and narrative-rich media creation

If you want, I can next provide one of these:
1. a more complete **TypeScript project skeleton**
2. a **JSON schema** for scenes/templates/policy envelopes
3. a **microservice diagram with APIs**
4. a **React editor proof-of-concept**
5. an **FFmpeg/export pipeline example**

